# The authority a program is handed, and the one effect there is so far.
#
# `Host` is a type nothing can build: its constructor is not among the names
# a term may use, so the only way to hold one is to have been handed it by
# `main!`. An effect takes it, which is what makes the authority show up in
# every signature that passes it along.
#
# The `!` says a name may do observable work. A pure name may not call one.
# Nothing declares `exit!`: it is the interface to the outside, so the
# compiler knows the name and a target answers for it.

type Nat Zero Succ(Nat)

add(a Zero) -> a
add(a Succ(k)) -> Succ(add(a k))

main!(h) ->
  two = Succ(Succ(Zero))
  exit!(h add(two two))
